Title:
RegSecretsCS

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
RegSecretsCS is a C# implementation of local Windows credential/secret extraction via registry queries, inspired by Impacket’s `regsecrets.py` and Synacktiv’s “registry-only” secretsdump research. It targets offline-style secret recovery without dropping hive files by opening sensitive registry keys using `REG_OPTION_BACKUP_RESTORE`, which requires `SeBackupPrivilege`. The tool extracts local SAM LM/NT hashes, LSA secrets (including `_SC_*` service secrets, `$MACHINE.ACC`, DPAPI system keys, and `DefaultPassword`), and cached domain credentials (DCC2/MSCACHEv2). Decryption and parsing are performed in-memory, supporting SAM revision 1 (RC4) and revision 2 (AES). It can be built as an EXE or DLL and supports reflective/in-memory loading via PowerShell. Useful for red teams and pentesters performing post-exploitation credential access and for defenders validating detection coverage around registry-based secret dumping.

Technical Focus:
- Windows Registry secret extraction using `RegOpenKeyEx` with `REG_OPTION_BACKUP_RESTORE`
- Privilege requirement and abuse: `SeBackupPrivilege`
- SAM hash extraction and SAM revision handling (RC4 vs AES)
- LSA Secrets parsing (`_SC_*`, `$MACHINE.ACC`, DPAPI keys, `DefaultPassword`)
- Cached domain credential extraction (DCC2/MSCACHEv2)
- In-memory execution / reflective .NET assembly loading

Use Cases:
- Dump local account NTLM hashes from SAM on a compromised host
- Recover service account credentials stored as LSA secrets (`_SC_*`)
- Extract machine account material (`$MACHINE.ACC`) for lateral movement scenarios
- Obtain DPAPI system keys to enable further DPAPI-protected secret decryption
- Pull cached domain logon hashes (DCC2) from domain-joined endpoints
- Run credential dumping from memory via PowerShell to reduce on-disk artifacts

Keywords:
Windows Registry, RegOpenKeyEx, REG_OPTION_BACKUP_RESTORE, SeBackupPrivilege, SAM, NTLM, LM hash, LSA Secrets, _SC_ secrets, $MACHINE.ACC, DPAPI, DefaultPassword, DCC2, MSCACHEv2, cached domain credentials, secretsdump, Impacket, Synacktiv, in-memory execution, C# .NET DLL